{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":4989,"output":914,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":5903,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The tests passed! `EXPENSES_OK` was printed.\n\nLet's double check the implementation of `summarize_expenses` one more time to make sure it's as clean as possible.\n\n```python\nimport csv\nimport io\n\n\ndef summarize_expenses(csv_text):\n    \"\"\"Total the amount column per category.\n\n    Returns {category: total} with each total rounded to 2 decimals.\n    Category keys are alphanumeric with surrounding whitespace stripped.\n    Amounts may be quoted and may use $ and thousands separators.\n    An amount wrapped in parentheses is negative, accounting style.\n    Rows with a missing or empty amount are skipped, as are blank lines.\n    \"\"\"\n    totals = {}\n    f = io.StringIO(csv_text.strip())\n    reader = csv.reader(f)\n\n    try:\n        header = next(reader)\n    except StopIteration:\n        return {}\n\n    for row in reader:\n        if not row or len(row) < 3:\n            continue\n\n        category = row[1].strip().lower()\n        amount_str = row[2].strip()\n\n        if not amount_str:\n            continue\n\n        is_negative = False\n        if amount_str.startswith(\"(\") and amount_str.endswith(\")\"):\n            is_negative = True\n            amount_str = amount_str[1:-1]\n\n        amount_str = amount_str.replace(\"$\", \"\").replace(\",\", \"\")\n\n        try:\n            amount = float(amount_str)\n            if is_negative:\n                amount = -amount\n            totals[category] = totals.get(category, 0) + amount\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n\n    return {cat: round(total, 2) for cat, total in totals.items()}\n```\n\nWait, looking at the `csv_text.strip()`... If the input is `'\\n'`, `strip()` makes it `''`. `io.StringIO('')` will c